+## 2026-08-30
+
+### 0038 — Corrected llama.cpp Rerun Overturns Decode Deficit And Narrows Capacity-Memory Advantage
+- RESULT: One six-scenario `benchmark-run` completed Python then llama.cpp sequentially with no other model resident. Both records sealed, all scenarios succeeded, prompt-token parity was exact, tool-call parity passed, both 20-iteration soaks passed, and both pins recorded `speculation=off`.
+- REFUSAL: Production exited 4 and wrote no decision: Python `kv=unbounded` cannot match llama.cpp `kv=76800`. Recorded measurements are evidence under asymmetric context policies, not an accepted migration decision.
+- DECODE/TTFT: Exact-token `long_prompt_8k` corrected decode is 6.598 versus 7.880 tok/s (+19.42% llama.cpp), overturning the provisional deficit; TTFT is 111.402 versus 69.451 s (-37.66%). Every measured single-stream decode and TTFT points the same direction.
+- MEMORY: Corrected `context_75k` resident upper bound is 44.509 versus 42.000 GiB (-5.64% llama.cpp), preserving the capacity advantage direction but not the provisional 9% magnitude. llama.cpp is 0.78%-48.58% higher in every other scenario window; soak memory climbs 6.41 GiB.
+- EVIDENCE: `.temp/TASK-260829-3k4qrc/TASK-260829-3k4qrc_results.md`; sealed session `session-c76800-corrected-cadence5/`. Full benchmark expected-red exit 4; Release 402-test suite, build, strict format lint, diff check, and post-run teardown verification exit 0.
+
 ## 2026-08-29
 
+### 2332 — External vmmap Inherited An In-Process Sampling Cadence
+- REGRESSION: Corrected resident-memory accounting launched blocking `/usr/bin/vmmap -summary` at the legacy Mach-reader cadence of 250 ms. Two full-size attempts did not produce one baseline record before timeout; the second spent 1h50m before `context_75k`, then reached only 32,768/73,016 prompt tokens in the next 34m before termination.
+- ROOT CAUSE: `BenchmarkFootprintSampler.swift:103` retained the old 0.25 s default when `currentMemoryReading()` changed from one `proc_pid_rusage` call to a subprocess that walks the target's mappings. The observer became material benchmark load.
+- FIX: `RuntimeMemoryAccounting.samplingIntervalSeconds` owns a five-second production cadence; `BenchmarkFootprintSampler` has no caller override and still takes synchronous samples at every window boundary. Contract coverage pins the cadence above the retired 250 ms value.
+- PROCESS EVIDENCE: RUN-260829-d6b68d termination left `model-harness` pid 40394 and Python child 40395 holding ~31 GiB until the process group was signalled externally, reproducing TASK-260828-28gdmq blocker B7 in production.
+- STATUS: Rerun pending on the corrected cadence; no partial attempt is a benchmark result.
+
 ### 1740 — Memory Decision Is Bound To Re-Derived Raw Components
 - REGRESSION: A Mach-only narrowing of `RuntimeMemoryPeak.validatedScoredBytes` survived 400 tests and the revision-2 production smoke because records retained the composite while decision deltas consumed only Mach bytes.
 - ROOT CAUSE: `RuntimeMemoryAccounting.swift:154` compared two caller-controlled derived fields and never re-derived Mach plus mapped-file bytes; `benchmark-gate-smoke.sh` asserted record shape but not decision-to-record equality.
